      <section id="introduction">
        <h1>Introduction</h1>
        <p>Wing is a Python CLI tool that exposes a local development server to the public internet through a shareable URL. It is designed to be simple to use, with no additional configuration required for typical workflows.</p>
        <p>Wing supports forwarding both HTTP and WebSocket traffic out of the box.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="cli-client">
        <h1>CLI Client</h1>

        <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
        <p>Wing's CLI client connects your development machine to the central relay. It forwards incoming requests to your local server and sends the server's responses back through the relay to the requesting client.</p>
        <p>The client is written in Python and requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>

        <h2 id="installing">Installing</h2>
        <p>Wing supports <strong>Windows, macOS, and Linux.</strong> Install it using the public installation script:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://wingserver.vercel.app/install.sh | bash</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>To verify the installation, run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>wing --version</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>The installer creates a dedicated Python virtual environment, installs Wing and its dependencies, and configures the <code>wing</code> command.</p>
        <p>If the command is not recognized after installation, restart your terminal or ensure that <code>~/.local/bin</code> is included in your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
        <p>For <strong>Windows</strong>, clone the repository to your machine. To run wing, you'll need to install the required packages which are specified under <code>requirements.txt</code>. To install the packages run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>pip install -r requirements.txt</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>After installing the required packages, to start using wing, run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>pip install -e .</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>You can verify installation by running:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>wing --version</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>or</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>python -m wing --version</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h2 id="updating">Updating</h2>
        <p>Updating Wing installs the latest release from GitHub. Run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://wingserver.vercel.app/install.sh | bash -s -- --update</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h2 id="uninstalling">Uninstalling</h2>
        <p>Uninstalling Wing removes its installed files, virtual environment, and command launcher. Any manual changes to your shell configuration may need to be removed separately.</p>
        <p>Run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>curl -fsSL https://wingserver.vercel.app/install.sh | bash -s -- --uninstall</code></pre>
        </div>

        <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
        <p>Wing can be started from any working directory. Flutter mode is an exception because it requires the path to a Flutter project.</p>
        <p>Use the <code>start</code> command followed by the port you want Wing to expose:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>wing start &lt;port-number&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>For example:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>wing start 8324</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>This exposes port <code>8324</code> for external connections. Wing provides a generated URL that can be shared to access the service over the internet.</p>

        <h2 id="flutter-support">Flutter Support</h2>
        <p>Wing includes a Flutter-specific mode for previewing Flutter applications. It builds a web version of your Flutter app, so make sure your project is configured to support Flutter web builds.</p>
        <p>See the <a href="https://docs.flutter.dev/platform-integration/web/building" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official Flutter web build documentation</a> for instructions.</p>
        <p>To run Flutter mode, use:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>wing start -f &lt;path-to-your-flutter-project&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>You can specify the path to your Flutter project or use <code>.</code> to reference the current directory. For example, if you're already in your Flutter project's directory, run:</p>
        <div class="code-block">
          <button class="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy code">
            <svg class="icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2" /><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1" /></svg>
            <svg class="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5" /></svg>
          </button>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>wing start -f .</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>In Flutter mode, Wing automatically runs a Flutter build command from your project and serves the project through a web server on port <code>8374</code>.</p>
        <p><strong>Note:</strong> Support for hot reloading is currently under development.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="contribution">
        <h1>Contribution and Support</h1>
        <p>Wing is an open-source project. Feel free to contribute to its development, use it, or modify it to fit your needs.</p>
        <p>If you encounter a bug, have questions about Wing's functionality, or simply want to get in touch, email <a href="mailto:gerenahu1@gmail.com">gerenahu1@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        <p>You can also open an issue in the <a href="https://github.com/nahugere/wing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wing GitHub repository</a>. When reporting a bug, please include a clear description and detailed steps to reproduce it.</p>
      </section>

